.SS "Comparisons to DirectX 11 Version"
.IP "\(bu" 2
No support for Visual Studio Directed Graph Shader Language (DGSL) effect shaders (i\&.e\&. \fIDGSLEffect\fP)\&. CMO files are loaded using BasicEffect or SkinnedEffect materials\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
VertexTypes does not include VertexPositionNormalTangentColorTexture or VertexPositionNormalTangentColorTextureSkinning which were intended for use with the DGSL pipeline\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBDirectX\fP Tool Kit for \fBDirectX\fP 11 supports Feature Level 9\&.x, while \fBDirectX\fP 12 requires Direct3D Feature Level 11\&.0\&. There are no expected \fBDirectX\fP 12 drivers for any lower feature level devices\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
The library assumes it is building for Windows 10 (aka \fR_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00\fP) so it makes use of XAudio 2\&.9 and WIC2 as well as \fBDirectX\fP 12\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBDirectX\fP Tool Kit for Audio, GamePad, Keyboard, Mouse, and SimpleMath are identical to the \fBDirectX\fP 11 version\&.
.PP
.SS "Release Notes"
FOR SECURITY ADVISORIES, see \fRGitHub\fP\&.
.PP
For a full change history, see \fRCHANGELOG\&.md\fP\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
In the June 2024 release, the defaulted parameter \fRinitialState\fP for the \fRCreateUploadBuffer\fP function in \fIBufferHelpers\fP was removed\&. Per the \fBDirectX\fP 12 validation layer, the only valid initial state for an upload buffer is \fRD3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_GENERIC_READ\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Starting with the February 2023 release, the Mouse class implementation of relative mouse movement was updated to accumulate changes between calls to \fRGetState\fP\&. By default, each time you call \fRGetState\fP the deltas are reset which works for scenarios where you use relative movement but only call the method once per frame\&. If you call it more than once per frame, then add an explicit call to \fREndOfInputFrame\fP to use an explicit reset model instead\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
As of the September 2022 release, the library makes use of C++11 inline namespaces for differing types that have the same names in the \fBDirectX\fP 11 and \fBDirectX\fP 12 version of the \fI\fBDirectX\fP Tool Kit\fP\&. This provides a link-unique name such as \fR\fBDirectX::DX12::SpriteBatch\fP\fP that will appear in linker output messages\&. In most use cases, however, there is no need to add explicit \fRDX12\fP namespace resolution in client code\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Starting with the June 2021 release, this library builds the HLSL shaders with Shader Model 6 via DXC\&. See \fRthis wiki page\fP for more information\&. The Microsoft GDK projects have always used Shader Model 6\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Starting with the June 2020 release, this library makes use of \fRtyped enum bitmask flags\fP per the recommendation of the \fIC++ Standard\fP section \fI17\&.5\&.2\&.1\&.3 Bitmask types\fP\&. This may have \fIbreaking change\fP impacts to client code:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
You cannot pass the \fR0\fP literal as your flags value\&. Instead you must make use of the appropriate default enum value: \fRAudioEngine_Default\fP, \fRSoundEffectInstance_Default\fP, \fRModelLoader_Clockwise\fP, \fRDDS_LOADER_DEFAULT\fP, or \fRWIC_LOADER_DEFAULT\fP\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Use the enum type instead of \fRDWORD\fP if building up flags values locally with bitmask operations\&. For example, \fRWIC_LOADER_FLAGS flags = WIC_LOADER_DEFAULT; if (\&.\&.\&.) flags |= WIC_LOADER_FORCE_SRGB;\fP
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
The UWP projects and the Win10 classic desktop project include configurations for the ARM64 platform\&. \fBBuilding\fP these requires installing the ARM64 toolset\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
When using clang/LLVM for the ARM64 platform, the Windows 11 SDK (\fR22000\fP) or later is required\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
The \fRCompileShaders\&.cmd\fP script must have Windows-style (CRLF) line-endings\&. If it is changed to Linux-style (LF) line-endings, it can fail to build all the required shaders\&.
.PP
